    "reasoning": "The target column 'Churn' is a categorical label indicating whether a customer churned, so the task is a binary classification problem. To establish diverse baselines we will train three models representing distinct modeling families: (1) Logistic Regression as a linear baseline; (2) Random Forest as a bagging ensemble of decision trees; (3) Gradient Boosting as a boosting ensemble of shallow trees. The execution layer will handle the required preprocessing: duplicate rows will be removed; missing values in 'MultipleLines' and 'TotalCharges' will be imputed; numeric features ('SeniorCitizen', 'tenure', 'MonthlyCharges', 'TotalCharges') will be standard\u2011scaled; categorical features will be one\u2011hot encoded; the identifier column 'customerID' will be excluded. A stratified train/validation/test split will be performed to preserve the churn class distribution. Each model will be trained on the training split, evaluated on the validation split using accuracy and weighted F1 (the only supported metrics), and finally tested on the held\u2011out test set. This plan provides baseline performance across linear, bagging, and boosting approaches without any hyperparameter tuning or advanced metrics."
